  "decision_conditions": [
    "The development hereby permitted shall begin before the expiration of three years from the date of this permission.\r\rReason: This is required by Section 91 of the Town and Country Planning Act 1990 (as amended).",
    "The premises shall be used only for educational use, and for no other use within Class F1 of the Town and Country Planning (Use Classes) Order 1987 (as amended), or succeeding legislation. \r\rReason: To protect amenity, in accordance with policies CS8 and DM10 of the LDF Core Strategy Adopted April 2012.",
    "The site and building works required to implement the development shall be only carried out between the hours of 08.00 and 18.00 Mondays to Fridays and between 08.00 and 13.00 on Saturdays and not at all on Bank Holidays and Sundays\r\rReason: To safeguard the amenity of the neighbours by minimising impacts of the development that would otherwise give rise to nuisance.",
    "The plant equipment hereby permitted shall only operate between the hours of 08:00 and 21:00 each day, as outlined in the Noise Impact Assessment prepared by Hann Tucker Associates, dated 19th August 2025. \r\r Reason: To safeguard the amenity of the neighbours by minimising impacts of the plant equipment during night hours.",
    "Prior to the occupation of the development, details of waste and recycling facilities to serve the development to which this permission relates shall be submitted to and approved in writing by the local planning authority. \r\rThe refuse and recycling facilities as shown in the approved details shall be provided prior to beneficial occupation of the development and shall be permanently retained thereafter. The developer and/or their successors in title shall take all reasonable steps to ensure that all refuse and recyclable materials associated with the development are either stored within these facilities or internally within the building(s) on the application site, and that no refuse or recycling material is stored or placed for collection on the public highway except on the day of collection.\r\rReason: To ensure proper waste management in the interests of the character and appearance of the area and the living conditions of neighbouring occupiers, in accordance with policy SI 7 of the London Plan 2021 and policies CS9 and DM10 of the LDF Core Strategy 2012.",
    "The development shall be carried out in accordance with the approved Fire Safety Strategy and thereafter maintained. \r\rReason: In the interests of fire safety and to ensure the safety of all building users, in accordance with Policy D12 of the London Plan 2021."
  ],
